# Adding a New Component

## Step 1 — Ask First
Before writing any code, ask:
- What category? (Power, Data, Production, Movement, Structure)
- What attributes and types?
- Size? (S, M, L)
- Require / conflict with other components?
- Custom API methods needed?
- Needs ItemStorage?
- Interacts with which system? (Power, Thermal, Items, CodeExecution)

## Step 2 — Search
```
scripts/components/         — existing components (avoid duplication)
include/game/systems/       — system integration points
web/src/components/frame/ComponentControls.tsx  — existing inspector patterns
```

## Step 3 — Create Lua Script
`scripts/components/<name>.lua` — follow existing component pattern.
Icon: white, no background PNG from game-icons.net → `assets/icons/`.

## Step 4 — System Integration (if needed)
- Power production/consumption → `src/game/systems/power.cpp`
- Heat generation → `src/game/systems/thermal.cpp`
- Inventory → `src/game/systems/items.cpp`
- Tick behavior → add to relevant system's `fixedUpdate()`

## Step 5 — Inspector UI (if needed)
Add controls to `web/src/components/frame/ComponentControls.tsx`.
Read the file first. Match existing patterns.

## Step 6 — Serialization (if new C++ data)
- Add to `COMPONENT_LIST` in `include/game/component_registry.hpp`
- Implement `field_save()` and `field_load()` with **matching fields in matching order**

## Step 7 — Verify
`just test-e2e` for C++ changes, `npm test` in `web/` for frontend.
